../../guards/codex-observe.md:21:- **Sequencing rule (amendment, 2026-11-15, Cycle 011 Condense — from deviation D1, priced as an escape by that cycle's codex-condense REVISE):** in a cycle-level firing, the seat files this call's return in the run directory BEFORE the jev-observe-exit judge for the same cycle is started, and the filed return is provided to that judge as part of its record. If the return is unavailable when the judge must start, the missing receipt is recorded explicitly in the run record (never silently absent). Founding incident: Cycle 011 Wave 9 — the seat filed the return while the judge was already running; the judge priced the absence as its Gap G4 and Plan had to cure it by receipt (RUN.md §2 P4, that cycle).
